<article class="env-lemma" id="063F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/063F">Lemma <span data-tag="063F">31.21.6</span>.</a> Any regular, Koszul-regular, $H_1$-regular, or quasi-regular sheaf of ideals on a scheme is a finite type quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows as such a sheaf of ideals is locally generated by finitely many sections. And any sheaf of ideals locally generated by sections on a scheme is quasi-coherent, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01IN" data-tag="01IN">26.10.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>